        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "A solution of Gd(beac)3·2H2O (0.03 mmol) in 15.0 mL of CH3CN was heated to 75 °C for 30 min, then a CH2Cl2 solution (5.0 mL) containing HL1 (0.03 mmol) was added. The mixture was stirred for another 4 h at 70 °C and then cooled to room temperature. After filtration, the resulting solution was kept in the dark and concentrated slowly by evaporation at 4 °C. After about 4 days, block-shaped yellow crystals were obtained. Yield: 38% (based on Gd).",
